Chiyo Film Terms of Use (End User License Agreement) — English translation
Last updated: 2026-11-13

This is an English translation of the Korean terms in LICENSE, provided for convenience. The
Korean text is the governing version; if the two differ, the Korean text prevails.

By installing or using Chiyo Film (including the editor app, the Photoshop plug-in, the Lightroom
Classic plug-in and the documentation and data provided with them; the "Software"), you agree to
the terms below. If you do not agree, do not install or use the Software.

1. License
The Software is a free test version. You may use it only for personal, non-commercial photo
editing. You own the rights to the photos you create with the Software, and you may use those
photos freely, including for commercial purposes.

2. Restrictions
You may not sell, rent or redistribute the Software (including the installer), modify, reverse
engineer or decompile it, or remove its copyright notices. When recommending it to others, please
point them to the official release page (https://github.com/chiyo-film/chiyo-film-release).

3. Ownership
The copyright and all other rights in the Software belong to the Chiyo Film developer. These terms
only permit the use described in section 1 and do not transfer any rights.

4. Disclaimer of warranty
The Software is provided "as is". To the extent permitted by law, no express or implied warranty
is given, including merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, freedom from errors or
uninterrupted operation. As a test version, results may differ from what you expect and files may
be damaged. Always keep your original photos backed up separately while using it.

5. Limitation of liability
To the maximum extent permitted by law, the developer is not liable for any loss of photos or
data, business interruption, or other direct, indirect or incidental damages arising from the use
of, or inability to use, the Software, except for damages caused by the developer's intent or
